Done. The inventory relay now serves `/health` over HTTPS without requiring a client certificate.

## What was changed

In `/etc/nginx/nginx.conf`, the single line in the `server` block was changed:

```diff
-        ssl_verify_client on;
+        ssl_verify_client off;
```

## Final configuration (`/etc/nginx/nginx.conf`)

```nginx
user www-data;
worker_processes 1;
pid /run/nginx.pid;
error_log /tmp/inventory-nginx-error.log notice;

events {
    worker_connections 512;
}

http {
    access_log /tmp/inventory-nginx-access.log;
    keepalive_timeout 10;

    server {
        listen 127.0.0.1:8443 ssl;
        server_name localhost;

        ssl_protocols TLSv1.2 TLSv1.3;
        ssl_certificate /etc/nginx/tls/server.crt;
        ssl_certificate_key /etc/nginx/tls/server.key;
        ssl_client_certificate /etc/nginx/tls/ca.crt;
        ssl_verify_client off;

        location = /health {
            root /srv/inventory;
            try_files /health.json =404;
            default_type application/json;
        }

    }
}
```

## Validation & reload

- `nginx -t` → `syntax is ok` / `test is successful`
- `nginx -s reload` → signal accepted, service still listening on `127.0.0.1:8443`

## Probe results (both trusting `/etc/nginx/tls/ca.crt`)

| Probe | Command | Result |
|---|---|---|
| **With** client cert (`client.crt`/`client.key`) | `curl --cacert /etc/nginx/tls/ca.crt --cert /etc/nginx/tls/client.crt --key /etc/nginx/tls/client.key https://127.0.0.1:8443/health` | **HTTP 200** — `{"status":"ok"}` |
| **Without** client cert | `curl --cacert /etc/nginx/tls/ca.crt https://127.0.0.1:8443/health` | **HTTP 200** — `{"status":"ok"}` |

Both requests succeed, confirming client-certificate verification is disabled while TLS remains enforced (TLS 1.2/1.3, server certificate from the local CA).
